# Pin text files to LF in the repository.
#
# The repo has always been LF, but a Git-for-Windows clone with the default
# core.autocrlf=true checks out CRLF, which produced ~420 phantom modified
# files in `git status` (zero real content changes) and broke
# scripts/test-line-item-order.mjs -- it extracts source by searching for the
# literal "\n  }\n", which never matches CRLF text, so build:check failed with
# `ReferenceError: orderedLinesWithIndex is not defined`.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect text vs. binary and normalize to LF in the
# index; `eol=lf` forces LF on checkout regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# NOTE: this is deliberately shipped WITHOUT `git add --renormalize`. Several
# claude/* branches are open and a repo-wide renormalization would conflict
# with all of them. Files normalize as they are next touched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats -- never touch these, even if content detection guesses wrong.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.mp4    binary
*.mov    binary
*.webm   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.zip    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.eot    binary

# SVG is XML -- text, despite living with the images.
*.svg    text eol=lf
